Apparently so. By default R is loading a number of packages (libraries) 
  when you just start it. The documentation has a toy example showing 
how to check where a symbol is coming from:
http://rpy.sourceforge.net/rpy2/doc/html/rinterface.html#r-packages-as-environments

Otherwise, the upcoming 2.1 version will be proposing a place where R 
packages can be given tailored python representations (that's still 
quite rough, but the earlier people try to break it the better).


